---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import ProductImage from './assets/whi-product.png'
---
<section class="bg-[#0A0A0A] text-white">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 grid gap-12 py-20 md:py-28 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-center">
    <Image
      src={ProductImage}
      alt="Where and How to Invest masterclass preview"
      class="w-full rounded-3xl border border-white/10 shadow-2xl"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <div>
      <span class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#FFBD40] mb-5">
        <span class="h-px w-6 bg-[#FFBD40]"></span>
        The solution
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl text-white">One focused session. A framework you keep forever.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-white/70">
        Where and How to Invest is a 60-minute masterclass taught by Oler Oladele, CFA — a securities trader with almost 20 years in Nigerian and global financial markets. It gives you the framework professionals use to decide where their money goes, applied clearly to your situation as a Nigerian investor.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        {[
          'Understand the investment landscape available to you — locally and globally.',
          'Learn how to evaluate any opportunity before committing your money.',
          'Walk away with a clear first step and the account setup guide to take it.',
          'Post-session email with accounts to open and introductions to relevant partners.',
        ].map((line) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">
            <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-[#FFBD40]" aria-hidden></span>
            {line}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
        <a href="#" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-[#FFBD40] px-6 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-black hover:brightness-95 transition">
          Start investing →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
